/E ( UPI Synchronization and "Offline" Trust:India leads the world in UPI, but integrating it into a mobile cart is tricky. If a customer scans a QR code on the cart's LCD to pay via PhonePe, but the store's internet blinks for three seconds, the cart might not receive the "Payment Success" signal. Current research lacks a fail-safe protocol for real-time payment synchronization on moving IoT devices. We need to solve how the cart can verify a transaction securely without making the customer wait for a "reconnection.")
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
402 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 173 0 R
/E ("Rough Handling" Gapl: Most global research focuses on building expensive, brand-new high- tech trolleys \(like the Amazon Dash Cart\). In India, retailers have millions of existing metal trolleys that are bumped, crashed, and left in dusty parking lots. There is a gap in ruggedized, low-cost retrofit kits. Research needs to focus on making a "brain box" that is cheap enough)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
