/T (3. Demographic Adoption and System Feedback The team gathered data on how different types of humans interact with the machine.  the learning curve is exceptionally flat; after just one "practice scan," any age group can master the system. Furthermore, interpreting the "accidental theft" data led to a crucial UI design choice: the system must correct human error quietly to maintain a "high-trust environment," rather than punishing the user with loud, embarrassing alarms. )
/E (3. Demographic Adoption and System Feedback The team gathered data on how different types of humans interact with the machine.  the learning curve is exceptionally flat; after just one "practice scan," any age group can master the system. Furthermore, interpreting the "accidental theft" data led to a crucial UI design choice: the system must correct human error quietly to maintain a "high-trust environment," rather than punishing the user with loud, embarrassing alarms. )
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [5]
>>
