756 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 193 0 R
/T (4. Macro-Level Store Intelligence \(Predictive Data\) The project interprets the cart not just as a billing tool, but as a moving data-collection node. Traditionally, a store only knows an item is sold after it passes the register. By interpreting the live cart data, the store gains predictive inventory intelligence. The manager knows the shelf will be empty before the stock actually runs out, allowing for proactive restocking and preventing "out of stock" disappointments for the next wave of customers.)
/E (4. Macro-Level Store Intelligence \(Predictive Data\) The project interprets the cart not just as a billing tool, but as a moving data-collection node. Traditionally, a store only knows an item is sold after it passes the register. By interpreting the live cart data, the store gains predictive inventory intelligence. The manager knows the shelf will be empty before the stock actually runs out, allowing for proactive restocking and preventing "out of stock" disappointments for the next wave of customers.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
757 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 193 0 R
/T (5. Hardware and Network Load Interpretation The technical timings in the code directly interpret the limits of the hardware.  The Raw Data: The ESP32-CAM is hardcoded to delay\(3000\) \(3 seconds\) between photos, while the user's mobile screen uses setInterval\(loadCart, 2000\) to refresh the cart every 2 seconds This data reflects a deliberate balancing act. If the camera took pictures instantly, it would overwhelm the store's local Wi-Fi and crash the server. By interpreting the network's bandwidth limits, the team introduced a 3-second delay to ensure stability, while keeping the UI refresh rate slightly faster \(2 seconds\) so the user never feels like the screen is frozen or lagging..)
/E (5. Hardware and Network Load Interpretation The technical timings in the code directly interpret the limits of the hardware.  The Raw Data: The ESP32-CAM is hardcoded to delay\(3000\) \(3 seconds\) between photos, while the user's mobile screen uses setInterval\(loadCart, 2000\) to refresh the cart every 2 seconds This data reflects a deliberate balancing act. If the camera took pictures instantly, it would overwhelm the store's local Wi-Fi and crash the server. By interpreting the network's bandwidth limits, the team introduced a 3-second delay to ensure stability, while keeping the UI refresh rate slightly faster \(2 seconds\) so the user never feels like the screen is frozen or lagging..)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
758 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 193 0 R
/T (6. Labor Reallocation The data does not interpret this as simply firing employees. Instead, it is interpreted as a massive Return on Investment \(ROI\) where human labor is reallocated. Employees are freed from acting "like robots" doing repetitive scanning and are moved onto the floor to help customers, making the store feel more human.. )
/E (6. Labor Reallocation The data does not interpret this as simply firing employees. Instead, it is interpreted as a massive Return on Investment \(ROI\) where human labor is reallocated. Employees are freed from acting "like robots" doing repetitive scanning and are moved onto the floor to help customers, making the store feel more human.. )
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
