1968 0 obj
<<
/Title (5. Hardware and Network Load Interpretation The technical timings in the code directly interpret the limits of the hardware.  The Raw Data: The ESP32-CAM is hardcoded to delay\(3000\) \(3 seconds\) between photos, while the user's mobile screen uses setInterval\(loadCart, 2000\) to refresh the cart every 2 seconds This data reflects a deliberate balancing act. If the camera took pictures instantly, it would overwhelm the store's local Wi-Fi and crash the server. By interpreting the network's bandwidth limits, the team introduced a 3-second delay to ensure stability, while keeping the UI refresh rate slightly faster \(2 seconds\) so the user never feels like the screen is frozen or lagging..)
/Dest [40 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1972 0 R
/Next 1964 0 R
>>
endobj
